<section class="section"><div class="container article-body">
  <h2>The Peanut Buster® Parfait: Six Decades of Layered Sundae Perfection</h2>
  <p>Long before high-speed spindle mixers brought Blizzards to drive-thru lanes, the <strong>Peanut Buster® Parfait</strong> established Dairy Queen as the premier destination for artisan ice cream craftsmanship. First added to the official national board in 1968, the recipe has remained purposely untouched for over half a century. While blended cups homogenize everything into a uniform puree, the parfait celebrates structural stratification: every plunge of the long red soda spoon yields a fresh collision of velvety frozen cream, piping-hot bittersweet fudge, and roasted peanuts with a brisk salty snap. Explore the full nostalgic collection on <a href="/categories/classic-treats">Classic Treats</a> or browse <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

  <h2>The Layering Blueprint: Why the Parfait Format Works</h2>
  <p>Unlike a standard sundae where toppings simply pool on top and leave unflavored soft serve underneath, the Peanut Buster Parfait follows a strict six-layer assembly cadence:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Bottom Anchor:</strong> A generous ladle of hot chocolate fudge lining the narrow base of the cup, insulating the first scoop of peanuts.</li>
    <li><strong>First Strata:</strong> Smooth vanilla soft serve crowned with a heavy blanket of whole salted roasted peanuts.</li>
    <li><strong>Mid-Tier Core:</strong> A second piping-hot ladle of cocoa fudge melting into the cold dairy, creating rich chewy ribbons.</li>
    <li><strong>Crowning Finish:</strong> A final tall swirl of soft serve topped with remaining warm fudge and a generous handful of crunchy peanuts.</li>
  </ul>

